# fzf colors, read via $FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS_FILE (see .zshrc). This starts from
# fzf's 16-color theme, so anything not set below follows the terminal palette.
# The rest follows nvim's snacks picker: orange matches, a red prompt and a
# light (fg1) border. The current line is bg2, a shade lighter than CursorLine
# so that it stands out from the gutter (the ▌ beside each other line), which is
# bg1. These gruvbox shades aren't ANSI colors.
--color=16
--color=hl:#fe8019,hl+:#fe8019,pointer:#fe8019,marker:10,prompt:9,info:8,header:8
--color=fg+:15,bg+:#504945,border:#d5c4a1,separator:#504945,scrollbar:#504945
--color=gutter:#3c3836
